    Bug 2009620 - Replace on-the-fly disabling of empty Recent/Favorites submenus with accessible stubs. r=aleca


    Previously, if the "Recent destinations" or "Favorites" lists were empty, the
    parent menu item was disabled on-the-fly as the user attempted to open it. This
    created a jarring user experience and caused accessibility issues, as screen
    readers lost focus and provided no context as to why the menu failed to open.

    This commit allows the submenus to open even when empty and populates them with
    a localized, disabled stub menu item (e.g., "(No recent destinations)").

    - Adds localized strings to messenger.ftl for the empty states.
    - Modifies folder-menupopup.js to build an aria-disabled="true" stub item
      instead of disabling the parent menu.
    - Introduces a .stub-menuitem CSS class in folderMenus.css to display an info
      icon, preserving the native menu icon layout and spacing.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D294125

diff --git a/mail/base/test/browser/widgets/browser_folderMenuPopup.js b/mail/base/test/browser/widgets/browser_folderMenuPopup.js
